166
00:11:18,100 --> 00:11:19,420
勾住排气管
Look, he's hanging from the tail pipe!

167
00:11:21,300 --> 00:11:23,900
还说不表演杂技
And he said he wasn't gonna do any stunts.

168
00:11:27,453 --> 00:11:29,171
天哪!
Holy cow!

169
00:11:40,860 --> 00:11:42,640
找不着他
I couldn't find him anywhere.

170
00:11:42,940 --> 00:11:44,600
他堕崖了？
You don't think he went over the cliff, do you?

171
00:11:44,600 --> 00:11:47,770
我们有更多排骨吃了
Well, if he did, that means more ribs for us.

172
00:11:51,077 --> 00:11:52,829
哥们，怎样？
Hey, guys. How's it going?

173
00:11:53,112 --> 00:11:55,831
天哪，还以为你死了
Gee, Seaver. We thought you bought it up there.

174
00:11:56,780 --> 00:11:58,260
你是说刚才的跳车表演？
You mean my trick dismount?

175
00:11:59,380 --> 00:12:02,620
你刚才难道是故意的？
You mean, you expect us to believe that you did that on purpose?

176
00:12:03,580 --> 00:12:07,080
当然了，你们是我朋友却那么笨
Yeah. Of course, I do. Look, you"re my friends. You're not all that bright.

177
00:12:11,760 --> 00:12:13,500
瞧他裤子背后
Look at the back of his pants.

178
00:12:14,840 --> 00:12:16,420
裤子背后怎么了？
What's wrong with the back of my pants?

179
00:12:17,240 --> 00:12:18,360
没有了
They're not there.

180
00:12:21,040 --> 00:12:22,880
还是让他看医生吧
We better go home and get him to a doctor.

181
00:12:23,020 --> 00:12:27,300
我没事，真的 我得歇一歇
No, no, man. Look, I'm fine, really. I just need to sit down for a minute.

182
00:12:36,900 --> 00:12:39,060
请问你叫什么名字？
May I have your name again, sir?

183
00:12:40,100 --> 00:12:41,940
巴富米罗.麦曼纳斯
McManus. Bartholomew McManus.

184
00:12:43,980 --> 00:12:46,560
-巴富米罗先生 -叫我巴斯就好了
- Well, Bartholomew-- - Just call me Barth.

185
00:12:47,220 --> 00:12:50,040
好的，巴斯先生 医生马上就来
Okay, Barth. The doctor will see you in a moment.

186
00:12:50,140 --> 00:12:52,080
-请坐 -好的
- Why don't you just have a seat? - Okay.

187
00:12:53,620 --> 00:12:55,300
不了，我坐一整天了
No, no, I sit all day.

188
00:12:56,400 --> 00:12:58,100
我需要克兰登的X光照片.
I'll need Mrs. Cramden's x-rays....

189
00:13:00,080 --> 00:13:02,920
-麦克!麦克.西弗 -麦克斯基医生？
- Michael! Michael Seaver. - Dr. McCloskey!

190
00:13:03,100 --> 00:13:05,000
周末也上班？
Look, I didn't think you worked on weekends.

191
00:13:05,180 --> 00:13:07,780
-不是有代班医生吗？ -埃米特医生？
- Don't you have that substitute doctor? - Oh, you mean Dr. Emmett?

192
00:13:07,920 --> 00:13:09,520
你本周放假
No, he's on vacation this week.

193
00:13:10,100 --> 00:13:12,420
你这么忙，我改天再来吧
You must be very busy. Look, I'll come back some other time.

194
00:13:12,491 --> 00:13:15,300
胡说，上来
Nonsense, nonsense. Jump up here.

195
00:13:15,300 --> 00:13:16,400
什么事了？
Now what seems to be the trouble?

196
00:13:19,300 --> 00:13:22,180
原来如此，让我瞧瞧
I guess that says it all. Well have a look.

197
00:13:23,480 --> 00:13:26,400
-破皮而已 -麦克，大事不妙
- It's just a little scratch, Doc. - That looks bad, Mike.

198
00:13:27,520 --> 00:13:28,820
分成两半了
It's broken in half.

199
00:13:34,800 --> 00:13:35,400
痛吗？
That hurt?

200
00:13:36,820 --> 00:13:39,380
不痛，刚才谁叫喊了？
No, no, not really. Was that you?

201
00:13:40,560 --> 00:13:41,940
怎么弄成这样了？
How did this happen, Mike?

202
00:13:42,354 --> 00:13:44,580
事实上，天生就是这样的
To tell you the truth, Doc, it's kind of always been like this.

203
00:13:44,580 --> 00:13:46,220
-我是装的 -麦克!
- It's just acting up. - Mike?

204
00:13:46,920 --> 00:13:49,700
好吧，好吧 我在派对里坐在热煎饼上了
Okay, okay, I was at a party and I sat on a hot pizza.

205
00:13:51,600 --> 00:13:53,380
看上去是擦破皮
Well, there seem to be some abrasions.

206
00:13:54,460 --> 00:13:55,560
那是烫伤
Those are cheese burns.

207
00:13:57,140 --> 00:13:58,500
那上面的肉汁呢？
And what about the gravel?

208
00:14:00,460 --> 00:14:01,580
没有叫肉汁煎饼
We didn't order that.

209
00:14:04,520 --> 00:14:07,020
我穿着内衣飞过纽约上空
So I'm flying over New York in my underwear...

210
00:14:08,160 --> 00:14:12,500
人们突然叫嚷.. “那个人内衣穿反了!”
and then, all of a sudden, people start yelling, "Hey, look! It's on inside out! "

211
00:14:14,020 --> 00:14:16,220
在你作为被遗忘的肯尼迪家族成员前.
Now, is this before or after the one where you we're...

212
00:14:16,440 --> 00:14:17,940
还是之后？
Ben, the forgotten Kennedy.

213
00:14:17,940 --> 00:14:20,960
之前，紧接着.
It was before that, and after the one...

214
00:14:20,960 --> 00:14:22,840
我变成一只人肉热狗后
where I turned into the human hot dog.

215
00:14:25,340 --> 00:14:28,060
本，我的报告要打分的
Ben, you know I'm getting graded on this paper.

216
00:14:28,100 --> 00:14:30,260
你没有瞎编骗我吧？
You're not just making this stuff up, are you?

217
00:14:30,540 --> 00:14:34,080
没有，这些梦都是真的
No, Carol. These are real dreams.

218
00:14:34,920 --> 00:14:35,740
敢发誓？
You swear?

219
00:14:36,842 --> 00:14:39,823
上帝可以作证，没有一个梦是编的
Cross my heart. I'd never make up a dream.

220
00:14:40,600 --> 00:14:44,540
这些材料足以.
Great. Well, this should be enough for a penetrating...

221
00:14:45,440 --> 00:14:48,380
深入分析本的心理世界了
psychological profile of the real Ben Seaver.

222
00:14:51,540 --> 00:14:53,600
深入且利润丰厚
Penetrating and profitable.

223
00:15:12,060 --> 00:15:13,860
杰森，你疯了？
Jason, you are crazy.

224
00:15:14,200 --> 00:15:16,200
因为我狂野？
Why, cause I was born to be wild?

225
00:15:16,820 --> 00:15:19,480
不，因为你把车开到我客厅里了
No, because you have a dirt bike in my living room.

226
00:15:20,780 --> 00:15:23,860
此刻，一个闷闷不乐的少年在山上.
Well, we also have a very unhappy boy up at Bear Mountain right now.

227
00:15:23,860 --> 00:15:27,040
我为什么不租一辆车教教他呢
So I thought why not go out, rent a bike, and teach him to ride myself.

228
00:15:27,840 --> 00:15:30,660
多美好，多可怕
What a sweet and incredibly terrifying idea.

229
00:15:32,040 --> 00:15:33,500
麦姬，我自有分寸
Maggie, I know what I'm doing.

230
00:15:33,560 --> 00:15:36,500
话说回来，我是骑哈利跑车长大的
I used to ride a Harley, for crying out loud.

231
00:15:36,880 --> 00:15:40,420
我知道，我还到医院探望你了
I know, sweetheart. I visited you in the hospital.

232
00:15:42,920 --> 00:15:45,220
当时平地冒出一头牛!
Hey, that cow came out of nowhere.

233
00:15:48,180 --> 00:15:49,460
-我要宰了你 -我也宰了你
- I'm gonna kill you. - I'm gonna kill you back.

234
00:15:49,682 --> 00:15:52,538
-你不能，因为你死了 -我慢慢死就行了
- You can"t. You'll be dead. - Not if I go slowly.

235
00:15:53,180 --> 00:15:55,940
等等，杀人的事交给我吧
Hold on. I'll do the killing around here.

236
00:15:56,660 --> 00:15:57,880
本搞砸了我的论文
Ben ruined my paper.

237
00:15:58,380 --> 00:16:00,620
<9岁儿童的梦境分析>？
Not the portrait of the sleeping 9-year-old?

238
00:16:01,060 --> 00:16:04,740
他说卖给我的梦都是真的
He said all the dreams he sold me we're real, and now I catch him...

239
00:16:04,740 --> 00:16:07,980
但我在院子里看见他跟拉夫买恶梦
on the front lawn buying a nightmare from Ralph Finsterwald!

240
00:16:09,160 --> 00:16:12,460
我说过梦是真的，没说梦是我的
Hey, I said they we're real dreams. I didn't say they we're mine.

241
00:16:13,439 --> 00:16:16,124
-本! -向朋友买梦不行吗？
- Ben! - So I bought a few off some friends.

242
00:16:16,320 --> 00:16:17,640
-我赚不了多少 -本!
- I barely broke even. - Ben.

243
00:16:19,140 --> 00:16:24,120
好吧，好吧，我有两倍的利润 这算是罪大恶极了吗？
Okay, okay, so I made a 200% profit. Is that such a crime?

244
00:16:25,440 --> 00:16:29,040
我的结论都没意义了，论文搞砸了
But you ruined my paper. Now all my conclusions are meaningless.

245
00:16:29,900 --> 00:16:33,220
凯罗，也许你可以借题发挥
I don't know, Carol. I think there might still be a paper in this somewhere.

246
00:16:34,360 --> 00:16:37,546
改成<罪恶的萌生>.
Say, the emergence of the criminal mind...

247
00:16:38,120 --> 00:16:42,500
或是<极刑的作用>，例如.
or the effects of swift and severe punishment, such as...

248
00:16:42,500 --> 00:16:45,360
整个周末帮姐姐干活
doing your sisters chores for a whole weekend?

249
00:16:46,280 --> 00:16:46,800
什么？
What?

250
00:16:47,773 --> 00:16:52,028
我看多于1周时间的数据才准确
I think it will take a lot more than a weekend to get reliable data.

251
00:16:52,180 --> 00:16:53,700
至少1周
I need at least a week.

252
00:16:54,380 --> 00:16:56,440
很好，本，你认为呢？
Sounds like a good idea to me. What do you say, Ben?

253
00:16:56,540 --> 00:16:57,660
我认为不好
I hate it.

254
00:16:58,660 --> 00:16:59,900
好吧，那就1个月
Okay, well make it a month.

255
00:17:00,300 --> 00:17:01,420
1周很公道
A week sounds fair.

256
00:17:03,500 --> 00:17:04,540
本，本.
Ben, Ben....

257
00:17:05,220 --> 00:17:07,280
千万别出卖自己的梦
Never sell your dreams.

258
00:17:08,040 --> 00:17:09,900
除非价钱很好
Not at these prices.

259
00:17:19,060 --> 00:17:21,540
-麦克？ -吗
- Mike? - Mom!

260
00:17:23,980 --> 00:17:26,160
你更苗条了!
Have you lost weight!

261
00:17:27,540 --> 00:17:29,000
你在这干什么？
What are you doing here?

262
00:17:29,940 --> 00:17:32,060
在这干什么？
Here? Here, Mom?

263
00:17:33,880 --> 00:17:36,600
那我问你：我们在这里干什么？
Let me ask you this: What are any of us doing here?

264
00:17:37,089 --> 00:17:41,173
这是个永恒的问题 某已故哲学家说过.
I mean, it's a timeless question. I think a dead philosopher once said--

265
00:17:41,640 --> 00:17:43,640
-麦克，你在这干什么？ -爸爸!
- Mike, what are you doing here? - Dad!

266
00:17:45,660 --> 00:17:46,800
你更苗条了!
Have you lost weight?

267
00:17:48,300 --> 00:17:50,120
怎么提早一天回来了？
Mike, how come you're home a day early?

268
00:17:52,740 --> 00:17:54,220
事实上.
Well, to tell you the truth, Mom...

269
00:17:54,220 --> 00:17:56,060
我和邦纳吵架了
I kind of got in a little argument with Boner.

270
00:17:57,040 --> 00:17:59,400
真遗憾，但回家就好
I'm sorry to hear that, but I'm glad you're home, Mike...

271
00:17:59,812 --> 00:18:02,224
我有惊喜给你
cause I have a surprise for you.

272
00:18:02,700 --> 00:18:04,360
来看看
Come on, take a look.

273
00:18:06,218 --> 00:18:09,199
麦克，怎么这样走路
Mike, how come you're walking like that?

274
00:18:10,120 --> 00:18:13,200
保持神秘感嘛
I'm just trying to keep the suspense alive, Mom.

275
00:18:18,864 --> 00:18:22,050
就在这里!不是重型机车是什么？
There she is, Mike! Is that a mean machine, or what?

276
00:18:23,260 --> 00:18:26,320
这是大岛705型 看过这种宝贝没有？
It is the Oshima 705. You ever see one of these babies?

277
00:18:27,160 --> 00:18:28,860
看过一次，相反方向驶过
Yeah, once. it was going the other way.

278
00:18:29,820 --> 00:18:32,360
这是你爸周末租的 他会教你怎么骑
Your father rented it for the weekend so he could teach you how to ride.

279
00:18:32,360 --> 00:18:35,200
好爸爸，好朋友，好家伙
Oh, gee! What a dad. What a pal. What a guy.

280
00:18:37,280 --> 00:18:38,720
我要睡觉了
Well, I'm off to bed now.

281
00:18:39,451 --> 00:18:41,396
麦克
Mike, bike.

282
00:18:41,900 --> 00:18:44,660
-上来试试 -试什么？在哪？
- Come on, plant that duff up here. - Which duff? Where?

283
00:18:45,757 --> 00:18:48,635
麦克!来!上车!
Come on, Mike! et's go! Hop on!

284
00:18:50,440 --> 00:18:51,480
真舒服
Ah, comfortable.

285
00:18:53,332 --> 00:18:56,620
快坐下，又不会咬你
Come on, sit down. It's not going to bite you.

286
00:18:56,880 --> 00:18:58,420
避震很好
It's got great suspension, too.

287
00:19:03,375 --> 00:19:05,229
看来他很喜欢
Maggie, I think he likes it.

288
00:19:09,581 --> 00:19:12,095
我感到迎面吹来的风了
I can feel the wind in our hair already.

289
00:19:12,620 --> 00:19:15,280
-杰森，过来聊两句 -爸爸，快聊
- Jason, might I have a word with you? - Yeah, Dad, have words.

290
00:19:15,340 --> 00:19:16,340
慢慢聊
Have lots of words.

291
00:19:17,740 --> 00:19:19,560
还是聊天比较好
Nothing that says it quite like words.

292
00:19:26,098 --> 00:19:29,352
杰森，麦克斯基医生打来了
Jason, that was Dr. McCloskey on the phone.

293
00:19:29,500 --> 00:19:32,060
-麦克今天找他了 -找他干嘛？
- Seems Mike stopped by there today. - Yeah? What for?

294
00:19:32,720 --> 00:19:36,620
臀部破皮淤青
Turns out he has some pretty bad bruises and abrasions on his gluteal region.

295
00:19:37,940 --> 00:19:38,940
麦克怎么不告诉我们？
Why didn't he tell us?

296
00:19:44,160 --> 00:19:47,300
这伤有可能是.
Now, could these be the kind of bruises that you get from...

297
00:19:47,720 --> 00:19:49,120
摩托飞车造成的？
say, falling off a dirt bike?

298
00:19:49,740 --> 00:19:52,460
我也这样问麦克斯基医生
I just happened to ask Dr. McCloskey the same question.

299
00:19:52,700 --> 00:19:53,560
他怎么说？
And he said?

300
00:19:53,880 --> 00:19:56,360
“不然就是刮毛严重失误”
It's either that, or a freak shaving accident.

301
00:20:00,820 --> 00:20:01,940
麦克!
Oh, Mike!

302
00:20:03,760 --> 00:20:04,600
爸爸？
Yeah, Dad?

303
00:20:04,980 --> 00:20:07,580
-准备好去骑车没？ -现在？
- Ready to go biking? - Now, Dad?

304
00:20:08,320 --> 00:20:11,320
对，来吧，咱们骑这玩意.
Yeah. Come on. We're gonna take this little puppy over...

305
00:20:11,320 --> 00:20:13,000
逛逛纽约最崎岖的地方
some of the roughest terrain on Long Island.

306
00:20:13,580 --> 00:20:16,540
你爸找了一天的坑洼地
You know, your father was out all day scouting for potholes.

307
00:20:17,180 --> 00:20:18,400
-坑洼地？ -是的
- Potholes? - Yeah.

308
00:20:18,600 --> 00:20:21,240
是男人的话就不用垫子
And if you we're real men, you'd do it without shock absorbers.

309
00:20:22,087 --> 00:20:24,601
拿下来怎么样？
et's take them off, Mike. What do you say?

310
00:20:24,980 --> 00:20:28,880
不，不要了，骑摩托车是很危险的
No, Dad, I don't think we should do this. I mean, dirt bikes are death machines.

311
00:20:29,900 --> 00:20:31,640
人们常常摔伤
People fall off and get hurt.

312
00:20:33,432 --> 00:20:36,515
不可能，只有傻瓜才会摔伤
No way. No. Only a bone-brain would fall off.

313
00:20:38,280 --> 00:20:40,760
屁股坐上来，咱们走
Come on. Let's get your rear in gear. Let's go, Mike.

314
00:20:40,780 --> 00:20:41,740
来吗，麦克!
Come on, Mike!

315
00:20:42,220 --> 00:20:43,820
别逼我了
Look, please don't make me.

316
00:20:45,040 --> 00:20:46,180
为什么？
But why not?

317
00:20:48,740 --> 00:20:50,640
因为我是个傻瓜
Because I'm a bone-brain, all right?

318
00:20:52,260 --> 00:20:54,540
我骑这个时摔下来了
I mean, I fell off one of these things at Bear Mountain.

319
00:20:55,000 --> 00:20:57,480
我答应过不骑，但出尔反尔 结果受伤了
I promised I wouldn't ride it, but I did, and I got hurt.

320
00:20:57,920 --> 00:21:01,900
我没有理会你的警告 你说对了，你们总是对的
You warned me, I didn't listen to you. You we're right. You're always right.

321
00:21:02,300 --> 00:21:03,880
我个人很讨厌这一点
And personally, I find that annoying.

322
00:21:06,040 --> 00:21:07,500
你们是怎么了？
What is it with you people?

323
00:21:08,480 --> 00:21:11,000
杰森，我们是怎么了？
I don't know, Jason. What is it with us people?

324
00:21:11,260 --> 00:21:13,140
因为我们年长 这个我们也无法控制
We can't help it. We're older.

325
00:21:14,380 --> 00:21:15,320
我们更有智慧
We're wiser.

326
00:21:15,940 --> 00:21:17,840
这点也很讨厌
I find that annoying, too.

327
00:21:18,920 --> 00:21:19,860
先听我说完
Then wait till you hear this.

328
00:21:20,600 --> 00:21:23,900
你得留在房间里一周
I think we agree that you should spend the next week in your room.

329
00:21:25,320 --> 00:21:27,140
我可以趴着吗？
Can I spend it lying on my face?

330
00:21:29,580 --> 00:21:30,220
可以
All right.

331
00:21:31,720 --> 00:21:31,980
谢谢
Thanks.

332
00:21:32,658 --> 00:21:33,943
麦克.
And, Mike...

333
00:21:35,080 --> 00:21:38,400
我们生气不是因为你骑摩托车.
what really upsets us is not just that you went and rode the dirt bike...

334
00:21:38,400 --> 00:21:40,080
而是你想要骗我们
but that you tried to deceive us.

335
00:21:40,399 --> 00:21:42,652
受伤了就要告诉我们
I mean, if you get hurt, we need to know.

336
00:21:43,360 --> 00:21:47,720
若是告诉你们就不用惩罚
Does that mean that if I had told you guys I wouldn't be punished?

337
